Declare gazelle's go_repository_config repo reproducible so it can use the repo contents
cache.

It only writes a config.json derived from its own attributes. Upstream already marks
`go_repository` and `go_repository_tools` reproducible but missed this one.
`bazel_gazelle_go_repository_cache` is deliberately left alone: it is a mutable cache.

Not yet raised upstream.

diff --git a/internal/bzlmod/go_repository_config.bzl b/internal/bzlmod/go_repository_config.bzl
index 97b69fa..75514f4 100644
--- a/internal/bzlmod/go_repository_config.bzl
+++ b/internal/bzlmod/go_repository_config.bzl
@@ -42,6 +42,12 @@ def _go_repository_config_impl(ctx):
         "dep_files": ctx.attr.dep_files,
     }))
 
+    # Bazel <8.3.0 lacks ctx.repo_metadata
+    if not hasattr(ctx, "repo_metadata"):
+        return None
+
+    return ctx.repo_metadata(reproducible = True)
+
 go_repository_config = repository_rule(
     implementation = _go_repository_config_impl,
     attrs = {
